course: dictionary
lesson: 7087
title: Payday and money words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Payday is the day when workers are paid their wages. Wages are paid by the hour, while a salary is paid for a whole year of work.
explain: Many families are paid once a month, so «Sometimes money runs out before payday.» The money is usually lowest just before pay arrives in the bank.
explain: Dad says, «Sorry bud, can't swing new ones till payday.» The clue is till payday: he cannot afford them yet, but he will be able to once his pay arrives. Can't swing means can't afford.
explain: A payday loan is a small, short-term loan with very high interest. It can be a money trap, because people often borrow again just to repay the first loan.
fact: Payday is the day when pay arrives, often once a month.
fact: Wages are paid by the hour, and a salary is paid for a whole year.
fact: Informally, a big payday means someone gets a lot of money at once.
fact: A payday loan is a costly, short-term loan that can trap people in debt.
fact: «Until payday» means until the day pay arrives.
exercise: «Sometimes money runs out before payday.» What does payday mean here? | A day in the week when the shops are shut | A day with no school | The day when money is spent on treats | *The day pay arrives
exercise: Dad says, «can't swing new ones till payday». What does can't swing mean? | Can't wait to play | Can't see clearly | Can't throw | *Can't afford
exercise: Why is money usually lowest just before payday? | Because people stop buying food | Because the bank closes early | *Because the pay has not arrived yet | Because shops give everything away for free
test: What is a salary? | A loan from a bank | *Money paid for a whole year of work | A gift at Christmas | Money paid for a single hour of work
test: What is a payday loan? | A free gift from the bank | A loan from a friend with no interest | A large loan that lasts for many years | *A small, short-term loan with very high interest
exam: A family says, «We got a big payday this month.» What does it mean? | The family went to the beach for the day | *Someone got a lot of money at once | The bank was closed all day | Someone was paid for a day at school
